---

## testsmells.org 19-Smell Academic Catalog — Audit Report

**File:** `OrderService.Tests/OrderProcessorTests.cs`
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 / .NET 10 | **Test methods:** 8 | **Smells found:** 10

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 4 | 4 |
| Medium | 5 | 4 |
| Low | 1 | all (fixture-level) |
| **Total** | **10** | **7 of 8 methods** |

---

### High-Severity Findings

#### 1. Conditional Test Logic *(Smell 1)*

**Test:** `ProcessOrder_SetsCorrectStatus` (line 24)
**Risk:** One branch is never tested — the test only verifies whichever path `TotalAmount` happens to take at runtime, silently skipping the other.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — if/else means only one assertion ever runs
if (result.TotalAmount > 100)
    Assert.AreEqual("PremiumProcessed", result.Status);
else
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
```

**Fix — split into two deterministic tests:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_StandardAmount_SetsStandardStatus()
{
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-CHEAP", 1) } };
    var result = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory).ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
}

[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_PremiumAmount_SetsPremiumStatus()
{
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-EXPENSIVE", 5) } };
    var result = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory).ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.AreEqual("PremiumProcessed", result.Status);
}
```

---

#### 2. Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test *(Smell 4)*

**Test:** `ProcessOrder_CompletesWithoutError` (line 43)
**Risk:** The test passes even if the processor silently corrupts data, returns garbage, or does nothing at all — any outcome short of an unhandled exception is "green."

```csharp
// ❌ No assertion — false confidence
processor.ProcessOrder(order);
```

**Fix — assert the expected side-effect:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_CompletesWithoutError()
{
    var processor = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory);
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-1", 1) } };

    var result = processor.ProcessOrder(order);

    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
    Assert.AreEqual("StandardProcessed", result.Status);
}
```

---

#### 3. Sleepy Test *(Smell 3)*

**Test:** `ProcessOrder_AsyncNotification_IsSent` (line 91)
**Risk:** `Thread.Sleep(2000)` adds 2 seconds of wall-clock time per run and is non-deterministic — on a slow CI agent the delay may be insufficient, causing flaky failures.

```csharp
// ❌ Arbitrary fixed delay
processor.ProcessOrderAsync(order);
Thread.Sleep(2000);
Assert.IsTrue(_email.WasNotificationSent(order.Id));
```

**Fix — use a polling wait or make the async API awaitable:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
