#### 8. Exception Handling in Tests *(Smell 8)*

**Test:** `ProcessOrder_EmptyOrder_ThrowsValidationError` (line 105)
**Risk:** The manual `try`/`catch` can silently swallow unexpected exception types (any non-`ValidationException` propagates as a test crash without a clear message).

```csharp
// ❌ Manual try/catch
try
{
    processor.ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.Fail("Expected an exception but none was thrown");
}
catch (ValidationException ex)
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Order must contain at least one item", ex.Message);
}
```

**Note:** This is the capture-and-assert variant (not a bare swallow), so it is functional. Still, MSTest has a cleaner built-in:

```csharp
var ex = Assert.ThrowsException<ValidationException>(
    () => processor.ProcessOrder(order));

Assert.AreEqual("Order must contain at least one item", ex.Message);
```

