#### 9. Assertion Roulette *(Extended Smell)*

**Test:** `CalculateTotal_ReturnsCorrectAmount` (line 70)
**Risk:** Three `Assert.AreEqual` calls with **no message parameters**. When one fails, the MSTest runner reports a line number but no semantic context — the developer must read the source to understand which value was wrong.

```csharp
// ❌ Three assertions, zero messages
Assert.AreEqual(247.50m, order.TotalAmount);
Assert.AreEqual(22.28m, order.TaxAmount);
Assert.AreEqual(269.78m, order.GrandTotal);
```

**Fix — add descriptive messages:**

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(247.50m, order.TotalAmount,  "Subtotal mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(22.28m,  order.TaxAmount,    "Tax mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(269.78m, order.GrandTotal,    "Grand total mismatch");
```

