### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** | Add meaningful assertions | Eliminates false-pass risk |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** | Split into 2 deterministic tests | Eliminates hidden dead-path |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** | `await` the async method | Removes 2s delay + flakiness |
| 4 | **Mystery Guest** | Inline CSV data | Enables CI portability |
| 5 | **Exception Handling** | Use `Assert.ThrowsException<T>` | Quick 3-line fix |
| 6 | **Eager Test** | Decompose or tag as integration | Improves failure diagnosis |
| 7 | **Magic Number + Assertion Roulette** | Named constants + messages | Improves readability |
| 8 | **Sensitive Equality** | Assert structured properties | Reduces formatting fragility |
| 9 | **General Fixture** | Remove unused `_logger` | Cleanup |

**Bottom line:** 7 of 8 tests carry at least one citable smell. The top four (Assertion-Free, Conditional, Sleepy, Mystery Guest) are high-severity and directly threaten test reliability. Fixing those four eliminates the false-pass and flakiness risks; the remaining medium/low items are readability and maintainability improvements.
